1
00:00:01,543 --> 00:00:03,963
MONICA, WHICH OF ALL
OF THIS KITCHEN STUFF IS MINE?

2
00:00:03,963 --> 00:00:06,256
THIS BOTTLE OPENER.

3
00:00:06,256 --> 00:00:07,257
AND...?

4
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:08,801
AND IT'S A MAGNET.

5
00:00:13,263 --> 00:00:14,431
GO ON.

6
00:00:14,431 --> 00:00:15,724
LOOK AT THAT.

7
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:17,559
HOW WEIRD IS THAT?

8
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:19,603
YOU KNOW,
YOU'RE MOVING IN WITH ME

9
00:00:19,603 --> 00:00:22,272
AND YOU HAVE THE ONE THING
I DON'T HAVE.

10
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:24,023
HUH? IT'S
LIKE, UH...

11
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:26,318
IN A WAY YOU,
YOU COMPLETE ME.

12
00:00:26,318 --> 00:00:27,361
YOU KNOW?

13
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:30,614
KITCHEN.

14
00:00:30,614 --> 00:00:31,615
WHAT?

15
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:34,242
YOU COMPLETE ME KITCHEN, MATEY.

16
00:00:35,661 --> 00:00:38,372
ROSS, I KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE THINKING.

17
00:00:38,372 --> 00:00:39,999
WHAT?

18
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:41,959
THAT SHE'S GOING
TO MOVE IN WITH YOU

19
00:00:41,959 --> 00:00:44,211
AND THEN MAYBE
SHE'LL FALL IN LOVE WITH YOU

20
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:46,672
AND THEN, WHEN SHE FINDS OUT
YOU'RE ALREADY MARRIED

21
00:00:46,672 --> 00:00:48,632
OH, SHE'LL JUST BE HAPPY,
YOU KNOW?

22
00:00:48,632 --> 00:00:50,300
YOU'RE JUST... YOU'RE VERY SAD.

23
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:54,053
OH... MY... GOD.

24
00:00:54,053 --> 00:00:56,473
I... I SEE WHAT THIS IS.

25
00:00:56,473 --> 00:01:00,310
YOU ARE IN LOVE
WITH RACHEL.

26
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:02,145
WHAT?!
OF COURSE.

27
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:05,106
IT ALL ADDS UP.
I MEAN, YOU'RE
OBSESSED WITH HER.

28
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:07,150
IT'S ALWAYS, "ROSS,
WHAT ARE YOU GOING
TO DO ABOUT RACHEL?"

29
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:09,653
"ROSS, WHY ARE YOU
MOVING IN WITH RACHEL?"

30
00:01:09,653 --> 00:01:10,821
"WHEN ARE YOU
GOING TO CONFESS

31
00:01:10,821 --> 00:01:12,406
YOUR SECRET MARRIAGE
TO RACHEL?"

32
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:14,950
YOU WANT HER.

33
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:15,993
NO!
( phone ringing )

34
00:01:15,993 --> 00:01:20,080
UH. OH, SAVED
BY THE BELL.

35
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,164
HELLO?

36
00:01:22,583 --> 00:01:23,918
HEY, RACH,

37
00:01:23,918 --> 00:01:25,460
AREN'T THESE
CANDLESTICKS MINE?

38
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:26,962
NO, NO, I BOUGHT THOSE.

39
00:01:26,962 --> 00:01:28,672
OH, RIGHT. I FORGOT...

40
00:01:28,672 --> 00:01:30,257
YEAH.

41
00:01:30,257 --> 00:01:33,010
( whispering ):
THAT YOU'RE A LIAR.

42
00:01:33,010 --> 00:01:34,177
Ross:
NO, NO.

43
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:35,178
THAT'S GREAT.

44
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:36,722
I'LL BE THERE MONDAY.

45
00:01:36,722 --> 00:01:38,933
AND THANK YOU
AGAIN. OKAY.

46
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:43,604
UM, THAT WAS THE HEAD
OF THE PALEONTOLOGY DEPARTMENT

47
00:01:43,604 --> 00:01:47,775
AT "N"... UH, "Y"... UH, "U."

48
00:01:47,775 --> 00:01:53,030
WOW. UH, WHAT...
DID HE... UH, SAY?

49
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:56,617
WELL, REMEMBER THAT
PAPER I HAD PUBLISHED
LAST YEAR ON SEDIMENT

50
00:01:56,617 --> 00:01:58,535
FLOW RATE? HUH?
THEY LOVED IT.

51
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:00,287
WELL, WHO WOULDN'T?

52
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:02,330
I KNOW.

53
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:06,627
ANYWAY, THEY ASKED ME TO BE
A GUEST LECTURER.

54
00:02:06,627 --> 00:02:09,337
I MEAN, IT'S TEMPORARY,
BUT, IF THEY LIKE ME

55
00:02:09,337 --> 00:02:11,506
IT COULD LEAD
TO A FULL-TIME JOB.

56
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:14,593
HOW GREAT WOULD THAT LOOK
ON THE MAILBOX, HUH?

57
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:15,761
PROFESSOR GELLER.

58
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:17,262
YEAH, PROFESSOR AND MRS.

59
00:02:19,431 --> 00:02:20,891
AND MRS.?

60
00:02:20,891 --> 00:02:22,684
UH...

61
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:24,937
OH, YEAH. YOU KNOW,
YOU AND ROSS ARE
STILL MARRIED.

62
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:27,773
WHAT?!

63
00:02:27,773 --> 00:02:30,025
JUST KIDDING.

64
00:02:32,987 --> 00:02:34,154
OH, GOD!

65
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:36,115
CAN YOU IMAGINE?!

66
00:02:36,115 --> 00:02:37,156
NO!

67
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:40,035
SAVED YOUR ASS.

68
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:52,589
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

69
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:54,842
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

70
00:02:54,842 --> 00:02:57,094
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

71
00:02:57,094 --> 00:03:02,099
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

72
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:04,309
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

73
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:06,561
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

74
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:10,858
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

75
00:03:10,858 --> 00:03:16,738
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

76
00:03:18,448 --> 00:03:19,700
HI.

77
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:20,909
( dejected tone ):
HI.

78
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:22,452
OH, WHAT'S
THE MATTER?

79
00:03:22,452 --> 00:03:26,289
WELL... YOU KNOW
THAT PSYCHIC I SEE?
YEAH.

80
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:28,917
WELL, SHE TOLD ME THAT I'M GOING
TO DIE THIS WEEK, SO I'M KIND OF

81
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:31,920
BUMMED ABOUT THAT.
WHAT?

82
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,130
YEAH, AND I KNOW
YOU GUYS DON'T KNOW

83
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:34,381
A LOT ABOUT PSYCHIC READINGS

84
00:03:34,381 --> 00:03:35,799
BUT THAT ONE IS PRETTY MUCH

85
00:03:35,799 --> 00:03:37,216
THE WORST ONE YOU CAN GET.

86
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:40,137
PHOEBE,
THAT'S CRAZY.

87
00:03:40,137 --> 00:03:41,763
I CAN'T BELIEVE
SHE WOULD SAY THAT TO YOU.

88
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:43,765
YEAH, HONEY, YOU DON'T
BELIEVE HER, DO YOU?

89
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:45,225
I DON'T KNOW.

90
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:47,227
SHE, YOU KNOW,
SAID THAT I'D HAVE TRIPLETS.

91
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,688
BUT SHE ALSO SAID
ONE OF THEM WOULD BE BLACK.

92
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:52,607
JUST OUT OF CURIOSITY,

93
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:54,317
DID SHE TELL YOU
HOW YOU'RE GOING TO GO?

94
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:55,777
NO, 'CAUSE SHE DIDN'T TELL ME
I WAS GOING TO DIE

95
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:57,487
TILL THE VERY END
OF THE SESSION

96
00:03:57,487 --> 00:04:00,074
AND I WAS NOT GOING TO WASTE
A WHOLE OTHER HOUR THERE.

97
00:04:00,074 --> 00:04:02,117
I MEAN, I'VE ONLY GOT
A WEEK LEFT, YOU KNOW?

98
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:04,953
I'VE REALLY GOT
TO START LIVING NOW.

99
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:09,290
HEY, EVERYONE.

100
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:10,792
OH, HI.

101
00:04:10,792 --> 00:04:13,545
HEY, UH, WELL, TODAY'S
MY FIRST LECTURE

102
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:15,589
AND I KIND OF WANTED
TO TRY IT OUT ON YOU GUYS.

103
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:16,548
DO YOU MIND?

104
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:20,802
NO, THAT'D BE GREAT.
OKAY. ALL RIGHT.

105
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:21,929
SURE.

106
00:04:21,929 --> 00:04:24,014
OKAY.

107
00:04:24,014 --> 00:04:25,224
( sighs )

108
00:04:25,224 --> 00:04:26,558
( humming nervously )

109
00:04:30,938 --> 00:04:33,690
( monotone voice ):
"THERE ARE THREE
PRIMARY THEORIES

110
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:35,817
"CONCERNING SEDIMENT FLOW RATE.

111
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:39,571
"EACH OF THESE THEORIES CAN
BE FURTHER SUBCATEGORIZED..."

112
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:43,491
OH, THIS IS IT.
THIS IS WHAT'S
GOING TO KILL ME.

113
00:04:45,284 --> 00:04:46,954
"SUBCATEGORIES:

114
00:04:46,954 --> 00:04:49,081
"THE FIRST
OF THESE SUBCATEGORIES...

115
00:04:49,081 --> 00:04:50,749
Joey:
UH, ROSS.

116
00:04:50,749 --> 00:04:53,794
ARE THERE, UH, ARE THERE NAKED
CHICKS ON THAT PIECE OF PAPER?

117
00:04:56,130 --> 00:04:57,631
NO. WHY?

118
00:04:57,631 --> 00:04:59,466
WELL, I JUST NEVER SEEN
A GUY STARE SO HARD

119
00:04:59,466 --> 00:05:01,885
AT A PIECE OF PAPER THAT
DIDN'T HAVE NAKED CHICKS ON IT.

120
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:04,138
OH.

121
00:05:04,138 --> 00:05:05,764
OKAY.

122
00:05:05,764 --> 00:05:07,015
OKAY.

123
00:05:09,476 --> 00:05:11,519
"THERE ARE THREE...

124
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:12,729
"PRIMARY THEORIES...

125
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:17,358
"CONCERNING SEDIMENT FLOW RATE.

126
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:20,946
"EACH OF THESE

127
00:05:20,946 --> 00:05:23,991
"THEORIES CAN BE
FURTHER SUBCATEGORIZED...

128
00:05:23,991 --> 00:05:25,867
"INTO...

129
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:27,953
WHY DON'T YOU OPEN
WITH A JOKE?

130
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:31,039
OPEN WITH A JOKE?

131
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:33,167
IT'S A UNIVERSITY,
NOT A COMEDY CLUB.

132
00:05:33,167 --> 00:05:35,961
WELL, WAIT A MINUTE.
HOLD THE PHONE.

133
00:05:35,961 --> 00:05:38,255
YOU'RE NOT TALKING
ABOUT CHUCKLES UNIVERSITY?

134
00:05:39,506 --> 00:05:40,715
OKAY.

135
00:05:40,715 --> 00:05:41,925
WE'RE KIDDING.
COME ON.

136
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:43,218
ROSS, HEY,
YOU KNOW

137
00:05:43,218 --> 00:05:44,678
WHAT MIGHT MAKE IT LESS BORING?

138
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:46,680
THANK YOU.

139
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:49,057
SOME, UM, SOME VISUAL AIDS.

140
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:50,934
OOH-OOH! YOU KNOW
WHAT'S A GOOD VISUAL AID?

141
00:05:50,934 --> 00:05:52,936
PLEASE DON'T SAY "NAKED CHICKS."

142
00:05:52,936 --> 00:05:54,855
WHY NOT?

143
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,564
YOU KNOW, I DON'T EVEN KNOW

144
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:59,734
WHY I BOTHER TO EVEN TALK
TO YOU GUYS ABOUT IT, YOU KNOW?

145
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:02,612
I'M JUST GOING TO DO IT
ON MY OWN WITH NO NAKED CHICKS.

146
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:05,490
THAT'S THE WAY I DID IT
UNTIL I WAS 19.

147
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:12,331
HI.
HEY.

148
00:06:12,331 --> 00:06:13,957
ANY GOOD MAIL?

149
00:06:13,957 --> 00:06:15,542
YES. YOU GOT SOMETHING
FROM THE SCREEN ACTORS GUILD.

150
00:06:15,542 --> 00:06:17,336
OOH. IT'S PROBABLY
A RESIDUAL CHECK.

151
00:06:17,336 --> 00:06:20,339
HEY, CAN YOU OPEN IT FOR ME?
I GOT A...

152
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:23,884
"BENEFITS LAPSED."

153
00:06:23,884 --> 00:06:25,302
HMM. THAT'S WEIRD.

154
00:06:25,302 --> 00:06:26,761
I DON'T REMEMBER BEING
IN A MOVIE CALLED

155
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:27,721
"BENEFITS LAPSED."

156
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:30,640
IT'S NOT A CHECK.

157
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:34,228
THEY'RE SAYING YOUR HEALTH
INSURANCE EXPIRED BECAUSE... 

158
00:06:34,228 --> 00:06:35,812
YOU DIDN'T
WORK ENOUGH LAST YEAR.

159
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:36,813
LET ME SEE THAT.

160
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:38,732
ALL RIGHT.

161
00:06:38,732 --> 00:06:40,399
OH, I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

162
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:42,736
THIS SUCKS.

163
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:46,156
WHEN I HAD INSURANCE,
I COULD GET HIT BY A BUS OR...

164
00:06:46,156 --> 00:06:47,782
OR CATCH ON FIRE, YOU KNOW?

165
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:49,326
AND IT WOULDN'T MATTER.

166
00:06:49,326 --> 00:06:51,245
NOW I GOT TO BE CAREFUL?

167
00:06:51,245 --> 00:06:53,288
I'M SORRY, MAN.

168
00:06:53,288 --> 00:06:55,498
THERE'S NEVER A GOOD
TIME TO HAVE TO...

169
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:57,209
STOP CATCHING ON FIRE.

170
00:06:58,919 --> 00:07:01,088
ALL RIGHT, WELL... I GUESS
I GOT TO GO GET A JOB.

171
00:07:01,088 --> 00:07:02,463
I'M GOING TO GO SEE MY AGENT.

172
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:04,132
OKAY, AND MAKE SURE
TO LOOK BOTH WAYS

173
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:05,842
BEFORE YOU CROSS THE STREET.

174
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:08,387
( sarcastically ):
MAKE SURE TO LOOK BOTH WAYS

175
00:07:08,387 --> 00:07:10,055
BEFORE YOU CROSS THE STREET.

176
00:07:16,353 --> 00:07:17,478
HEY.

177
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:19,480
HEY, PHEEBS, YOU'RE STILL ALIVE.

178
00:07:21,233 --> 00:07:23,110
HOW ARE YOU FEELING?

179
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:26,280
OH, IT'S SO EXHAUSTING
WAITING FOR DEATH.

180
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,865
OH, BY THE WAY,
DO YOU THINK...

181
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,909
( gasping )

182
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:33,828
PHEEBS, WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

183
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:36,123
I WAS PREPARING YOU
FOR MY DE...

184
00:07:36,123 --> 00:07:37,916
DIDN'T YOU THINK I WAS DEAD?

185
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:39,293
DID THAT NOT COME OFF?

186
00:07:39,293 --> 00:07:41,378
NO. YEAH,
SCARED THE HELL OUT OF ME.

187
00:07:41,378 --> 00:07:43,797
I THOUGHT
WE'D LOST YOU FOREVER.

188
00:07:43,797 --> 00:07:45,382
PHEEBS, YOU WANT TO LIE DOWN?

189
00:07:45,382 --> 00:07:47,092
YEAH. THANKS.

190
00:07:47,092 --> 00:07:49,803
AND, LISTEN,
CAN YOU DO ME A FAVOR?

191
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:52,389
CAN YOU JUST, UH, WAKE ME UP
IN A COUPLE HOURS--

192
00:07:52,389 --> 00:07:53,640
YOU KNOW, IF YOU CAN?

193
00:07:57,352 --> 00:07:58,770
MONICA...

194
00:08:01,815 --> 00:08:03,650
DID-DID YOU TAKE THESE BACK?

195
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:05,986
NO, NO.
I JUST... I LIKED THEM SO MUCH

196
00:08:05,986 --> 00:08:08,696
THAT I WENT OUT
AND BOUGHT SOME FOR MYSELF.

197
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:11,158
OH. YEAH, THEY'RE
REALLY GREAT, AREN'T THEY?

198
00:08:11,158 --> 00:08:12,742
I LOVE THEM.

199
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:13,827
YEAH.

200
00:08:13,827 --> 00:08:14,953
NICE TRY.

201
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:18,623
HELLO.

202
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:20,000
HEY. HOW'D THE LECTURE GO?

203
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,002
IT WENT GREAT.

204
00:08:22,002 --> 00:08:26,423
AND I DIDN'T NEED ANY JOKES
OR NAKED CHICKS EITHER.

205
00:08:26,423 --> 00:08:28,133
WOW. THAT'S GREAT, ROSS.

206
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:29,676
I'M SORRY WE WEREN'T
MORE SUPPORTIVE BEFORE.

207
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:31,345
I KNEW ALL I HAD TO DO WAS LET

208
00:08:31,345 --> 00:08:33,096
THE MATERIAL SPEAK
FOR ITSELF, HUH?

209
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:34,473
EVERYONE'S ALL, UH

210
00:08:34,473 --> 00:08:36,599
"ROSS, YOU HAVE TO BE
FUNNY AND SEXY."

211
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:38,643
WELL, I PROVED THEM WRONG.

212
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:40,312
AND NOW,

213
00:08:40,312 --> 00:08:42,689
I'M GOING TO PASS THE NEWS ON
TO JOEY AND CHANDLER.

214
00:08:42,689 --> 00:08:44,149
THAT YOU'RE NOT FUNNY
OR SEXY?

215
00:08:44,149 --> 00:08:45,525
THAT'S RIGHT.

216
00:08:51,031 --> 00:08:53,325
HEY, ESTELLE,
LISTEN...

217
00:08:53,325 --> 00:08:54,868
WELL, WELL, WELL.

218
00:08:54,868 --> 00:08:56,911
JOEY TRIBBIANI.

219
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:59,206
SO YOU CAME BACK, HUH?

220
00:08:59,206 --> 00:09:01,208
THEY THINK THEY CAN DO BETTER

221
00:09:01,208 --> 00:09:04,878
BUT THEY ALL COME
CRAWLING BACK TO ESTELLE.

222
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:08,340
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

223
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:09,757
I NEVER LEFT YOU.

224
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:11,426
YOU'VE ALWAYS BEEN MY AGENT.

225
00:09:11,426 --> 00:09:12,511
REALLY?

226
00:09:12,511 --> 00:09:13,720
YEAH.

227
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,055
OH, WELL.

228
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:17,224
NO HARM, NO FOUL.

229
00:09:17,224 --> 00:09:18,475
LOOK, ESTELLE...

230
00:09:18,475 --> 00:09:20,018
YOU GOT TO GET
ME SOME WORK.

231
00:09:20,018 --> 00:09:21,560
I LOST MY
HEALTH INSURANCE.

232
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:23,021
ALL RIGHT.

233
00:09:23,021 --> 00:09:26,274
FIRST THING WE GOT TO DO--
DAMAGE CONTROL.
WHY?

234
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:28,735
WELL, I THINK, UH...

235
00:09:28,735 --> 00:09:31,112
SOMEONE OUT THERE...

236
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:33,823
MAY HAVE BEEN BAD-MOUTHING
YOU ALL OVER TOWN.

237
00:09:36,451 --> 00:09:37,411
THAT BASTARD!

238
00:09:44,918 --> 00:09:46,044
HI.

239
00:09:46,044 --> 00:09:47,504
( in strained voice ):
HEY.

240
00:09:47,504 --> 00:09:49,005
SO ESTELLE

241
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:51,341
LINED UP A BUNCH OF AUDITIONS
FOR ME TOMORROW

242
00:09:51,341 --> 00:09:54,219
AND I'LL HAVE MY HEALTH
INSURANCE BACK IN NO TIME.

243
00:09:54,219 --> 00:09:56,555
THAT'S GREAT, BUT...

244
00:09:56,555 --> 00:09:58,848
SHOULDN'T YOU BE
ON THE TOILET RIGHT NOW?

245
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:02,936
WHAT?

246
00:10:02,936 --> 00:10:04,938
WHAT'S WRONG WITH YOU?

247
00:10:04,938 --> 00:10:06,356
NOTHING.

248
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:09,067
WELL, I GOT THIS BLINDING PAIN
IN MY STOMACH

249
00:10:09,067 --> 00:10:11,152
WHEN I WAS
LIFTING WEIGHTS BEFORE

250
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:12,820
AND THEN I, UH, PASSED OUT

251
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:15,115
AND, UH, I HAVEN'T BEEN ABLE
TO STAND UP SINCE.

252
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:16,908
( weak chuckle )

253
00:10:16,908 --> 00:10:19,578
BUT, UH, I DON'T THINK
IT'S ANYTHING SERIOUS, YOU KNOW?

254
00:10:19,578 --> 00:10:20,870
THIS SOUNDS LIKE A HERNIA.

255
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,747
YOU HAVE TO...
YOU GO TO THE DOCTOR.

256
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:25,708
NO WAY. OKAY, LOOK, IF I'M GOING
TO GO TO THE DOCTOR FOR ANYTHING

257
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:28,503
IT'S GOING TO BE FOR THIS THING
STICKING OUT OF MY STOMACH.

258
00:10:30,589 --> 00:10:32,215
( groaning )

259
00:10:32,215 --> 00:10:34,008
THAT'S A HERNIA.

260
00:10:34,008 --> 00:10:37,095
WHY'D I HAVE TO START
WORKING OUT AGAIN?

261
00:10:37,095 --> 00:10:39,055
DAMN YOU 15s!

262
00:10:42,934 --> 00:10:44,311
WELL, WE'RE A LITTLE EARLY.

263
00:10:44,311 --> 00:10:46,104
THE LECTURE DOESN'T END
FOR 15 MINUTES.

264
00:10:46,104 --> 00:10:47,688
YEAH, BUT, YOU KNOW, WE
COULD SNEAK IN AND WATCH.

265
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:49,941
YEAH. OH, HEY, LOOK.

266
00:10:49,941 --> 00:10:51,610
THERE'S SOME
KAPPA KAPPA DELTAS.

267
00:10:51,610 --> 00:10:53,111
I WAS A KAPPA.

268
00:10:53,111 --> 00:10:54,279
HEY, SISTERS.

269
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:59,700
WOW. WE REALLY ARE BITCHES.

270
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:03,704
( speaking with confident
British accent )

271
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:05,540
RIGHT. SO WHEN RIGBY
GOT HIS SAMPLES

272
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:06,833
BACK FROM THE LABORATORY

273
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:09,586
HE MADE A STARTLING DISCOVERY.

274
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:15,967
WHAT HE BELIEVED TO BE IGNEOUS
WAS, IN FACT, SEDIMENTARY.

275
00:11:17,469 --> 00:11:20,555
IMAGINE HIS CONSTERNATION
WHEN...

276
00:11:24,309 --> 00:11:26,561
OH, BLOODY 'ELL.

277
00:11:31,358 --> 00:11:34,319
Monica:
WHAT THE HELL ARE YOU DOING?

278
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:36,029
LOOK, I WAS NERVOUS.

279
00:11:36,029 --> 00:11:38,823
YOU GUYS HAD ME ALL WORRIED
I WAS GOING TO BE BORING.

280
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:42,410
I GOT UP THERE AND THEY WERE
ALL, LIKE, STARING AT ME.

281
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:43,702
I OPENED MY MOUTH

282
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:46,705
AND THIS BRITISH ACCENT
JUST CAME OUT.

283
00:11:46,705 --> 00:11:49,584
YEAH, AND NOT
A VERY GOOD ONE.

284
00:11:49,584 --> 00:11:52,337
WILL YOU PLEASE...?

285
00:11:52,337 --> 00:11:54,214
DR. GELLER, KURT RATHMAN.

286
00:11:54,214 --> 00:11:56,508
I'M A PROFESSOR IN
THE PALEONTOLOGY
DEPARTMENT HERE.

287
00:11:56,508 --> 00:11:59,052
DO YOU HAVE A MOMENT TO
TALK ABOUT YOUR LECTURE?

288
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:02,514
( British accent ):
I'M SORRY, I'VE GOT
PLANS WITH MY SISTER.

289
00:12:02,514 --> 00:12:04,891
( Irish accent ):
MONICA GELLER-R-R-R....

290
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:09,479
RIGHT. WILL YOU EXCUSE
US FOR ONE MOMENT?

291
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:11,272
( normal ):
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

292
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:13,274
( normal):
OH, YOU CAN HAVE AN
ACCENT, BUT I CAN'T?

293
00:12:13,274 --> 00:12:16,777
( Irish ):
TOP O' THE MORNIN'
TO YE, LADDIES!

294
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:19,072
WILL YOU JUST
PLEASE STOP?

295
00:12:19,072 --> 00:12:21,866
( Indian accent ):
YES, YES, BOMBAY IS

296
00:12:21,866 --> 00:12:24,327
VERY, VERY NICE
THIS TIME OF YEAR.

297
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:33,712
( grunting )

298
00:12:33,712 --> 00:12:36,506
( sobbing )

299
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:42,345
HEY, WILL YOU GRAB ME
A CRULLER?

300
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:44,598
( whining )

301
00:12:44,598 --> 00:12:46,891
SIT DOWN!

302
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:49,269
WILL YOU GO TO THE HOSPITAL?

303
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:53,398
DUDE, HERNIA OPERATIONS COST,
LIKE... A LOT, PROBABLY, OKAY?

304
00:12:53,398 --> 00:12:56,025
BESIDES, IT'S GETTING DARKER
AND MORE PAINFUL.

305
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:57,902
THAT MEANS IT'S HEALING.

306
00:12:57,902 --> 00:13:00,113
LOOK, I WILL LOAN YOU
THE MONEY.

307
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:04,158
JUST GO TO THE HOSPITAL,
AND LET'S JUST GET THAT THING...

308
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:06,494
PUSHED BACK IN?

309
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:08,747
THANK YOU, BUT IT WOULD
TAKE ME FOREVER

310
00:13:08,747 --> 00:13:10,749
TO PAY YOU THAT MONEY BACK,
AND...

311
00:13:10,749 --> 00:13:12,791
I DON'T WANT THAT
HANGING OVER MY HEAD, OKAY?

312
00:13:12,791 --> 00:13:14,877
AND BESIDES, AS SOON AS
MY INSURANCE KICKS IN

313
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:17,088
I CAN GET ALL THE FREE
OPERATIONS I WANT, OKAY?

314
00:13:17,088 --> 00:13:20,883
I THINK I'LL PROBABLY START WITH
THAT LASER EYE SURGERY THING.

315
00:13:22,427 --> 00:13:24,512
HEY...
HEY.

316
00:13:24,512 --> 00:13:25,972
( groaning )
HEY...
WHAT'S GOING ON?

317
00:13:25,972 --> 00:13:27,890
WELL, JOEY'S GOT
A REALLY BAD HERNIA

318
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:31,311
BUT IT'S NOTHING THAT A LITTLE
LASER EYE SURGERY WON'T FIX,

319
00:13:31,311 --> 00:13:32,937
LOOK, I'M TELLING YOU--

320
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:35,774
IF I PUT MY HAND
ON MY STOMACH RIGHT HERE

321
00:13:35,774 --> 00:13:37,609
IT DOESN'T HURT THAT BAD.

322
00:13:37,609 --> 00:13:39,860
HEY! MAYBE YOU'LL DIE.

323
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,906
CHANDLER, I'M SCARED.

324
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:45,950
NO, WE CAN GO
TOGETHER!

325
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:47,868
JUST DON'T WAIT TOO LONG,
THOUGH, OKAY?

326
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:50,121
'CAUSE I'M OUT OF HERE
SOMETIME BEFORE FRIDAY.

327
00:13:50,121 --> 00:13:52,791
YEAH, BUT I DON'T WANT TO DIE.

328
00:13:52,791 --> 00:13:54,334
NO, NO, IT'LL BE FUN.

329
00:13:54,334 --> 00:13:56,210
WE CAN COME BACK
AND WE CAN HAUNT THESE GUYS.

330
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:03,134
GIVE ME THEM!

331
00:14:03,134 --> 00:14:04,719
NO! THEY ARE MINE!

332
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:06,805
YOU STOLE THEM FROM ME!
YOU STOLE THEM FROM ME!

333
00:14:06,805 --> 00:14:09,182
GIVE ME THEM!
GIVE ME THEM!

334
00:14:10,642 --> 00:14:12,727
YOU JUST WANT TO EACH
TAKE ONE?

335
00:14:12,727 --> 00:14:16,773
YEAH, THAT SEEMS FAIR--
WE NEVER USE THEM.

336
00:14:16,773 --> 00:14:20,401
LOOK, I REALLY NEED
SOME HELP, OKAY?

337
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:24,489
WHY, WHY DID I HAVE TO SPEAK
IN A BRITISH ACCENT?

338
00:14:24,489 --> 00:14:26,073
WHAT DO I DO?

339
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:27,826
WELL... WHY DON'T
YOU PHASE IT OUT?

340
00:14:27,826 --> 00:14:29,327
YEAH, PHASE THE ACCENT OUT--

341
00:14:29,327 --> 00:14:31,371
PEOPLE WILL THINK THAT,
YOU'RE, YOU KNOW

342
00:14:31,371 --> 00:14:33,122
JUST ADJUSTING TO LIFE
IN AMERICA.

343
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,708
Rachel:
YEAH, COME ON, ROSS--

344
00:14:34,708 --> 00:14:36,292
NO ONE'LL EVEN NOTICE.

345
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:38,294
I MEAN, THEY'RE PROBABLY NOT
EVEN LISTENING TO YOU.

346
00:14:40,087 --> 00:14:41,922
THEY'RE NOT LISTENING TO ME?

347
00:14:41,922 --> 00:14:44,676
OF COURSE THEY'RE LISTENING
TO YOU.

348
00:14:44,676 --> 00:14:46,594
EVERYBODY LISTENS TO YOU.

349
00:14:46,594 --> 00:14:48,680
MONICA, UH,
YOU REALLY THINK I SHOULD TRY

350
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,473
THIS "PHASING OUT" THING?

351
00:14:50,473 --> 00:14:52,183
I THINK YOU LOOK FINE.

352
00:14:55,854 --> 00:14:56,979
WHENEVER YOU'RE READY.

353
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:58,439
OKAY.

354
00:14:58,439 --> 00:14:59,524
( groaning )

355
00:14:59,524 --> 00:15:01,735
HEY, TIMMY...

356
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:03,528
I'VE GOT A...

357
00:15:03,528 --> 00:15:05,739
SURPRISE... FOR YOU.

358
00:15:05,739 --> 00:15:07,657
HOLD IT, I'M SORRY.

359
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,534
THE SURPRISE IS
A NEW SWING SET.

360
00:15:09,534 --> 00:15:12,036
IF YOU COULD PLAY IT
A LITTLE LESS INTENSE?

361
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:14,038
YEAH, SURE. NO PROBLEM.

362
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:16,457
UH, JUST HOLD ON ONE SECOND.

363
00:15:17,542 --> 00:15:19,001
( groaning )

364
00:15:22,213 --> 00:15:24,924
HEY, TIMMY...

365
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:28,595
I'VE GOT A SURPRISE
FOR YOU.

366
00:15:28,595 --> 00:15:29,721
OH, MY GOD!

367
00:15:35,435 --> 00:15:39,480
...SO THAT'S WHY I FEED MY DOG
PURINA ONE.

368
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:41,608
PICK UP A BAG TODAY.

369
00:15:43,401 --> 00:15:44,861
THAT'S WHERE YOU
PICK UP THE BAG.

370
00:15:44,861 --> 00:15:46,780
EXACTLY.

371
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:51,325
NO, THE LINE IS "PICK UP A BAG,"
SO YOU NEED TO PICK UP THE BAG.

372
00:15:51,325 --> 00:15:52,410
OR...

373
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:54,662
I COULD JUST POINT TO IT, HUH?

374
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:56,873
"BLAH-BLAH-BLAH, PURINA ONE.

375
00:15:56,873 --> 00:16:00,877
POINT TO A BAG TODAY."

376
00:16:02,879 --> 00:16:04,923
I DIDN'T GET IT, DID I?

377
00:16:04,923 --> 00:16:07,675
NO.
YEAH, OKAY.

378
00:16:10,845 --> 00:16:13,389
HI. I'M, UH, JOEY TRIBBIANI.

379
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:15,391
I'M HERE TO AUDITION FOR "MAN."

380
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:16,768
( groaning )

381
00:16:16,768 --> 00:16:18,352
YOU MEAN "DYING MAN"?

382
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:20,855
YES!

383
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:24,024
OKAY, COME ON--
DO IT ONE MORE TIME.
REALLY? REALLY?

384
00:16:24,024 --> 00:16:25,735
YES!
OKAY.

385
00:16:29,656 --> 00:16:31,574
( Scottish accent ):
HELLO, ROSS?
THIS IS DR. McNEELY

386
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:33,367
FROM THE FAKE ACCENT UNIVERSITY.

387
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:36,913
WE'D LIKE YOU TO COME ONBOARD
WITH US FULL-TIME.

388
00:16:36,913 --> 00:16:38,456
( squealing )

389
00:16:39,749 --> 00:16:41,041
HEY!

390
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:42,543
HEY!

391
00:16:42,543 --> 00:16:43,962
LISTEN TO THIS--

392
00:16:43,962 --> 00:16:46,172
MY READING WAS WRONG;
I'M NOT GOING TO DIE.

393
00:16:46,172 --> 00:16:48,090
REALLY? HOW DO YOU KNOW?

394
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:49,592
BECAUSE MY PSYCHIC IS DEAD.

395
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:54,138
SHE MUST HAVE READ
THE CARDS WRONG.

396
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:55,723
OH... WELL, I'M SORRY.

397
00:16:55,723 --> 00:16:57,809
EH, BETTER HER THAN ME.

398
00:16:57,809 --> 00:16:59,268
HEY, LET'S BAKE COOKIES!

399
00:17:05,399 --> 00:17:07,944
LISTEN, I'M REALLY GLAD
YOU GOT THE PART.

400
00:17:07,944 --> 00:17:09,487
( groaning )

401
00:17:09,487 --> 00:17:12,239
BUT ARE YOU SURE
YOU CAN DO THIS?

402
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:15,493
YEAH! AND, HEY, MAN,
THANKS FOR COMING WITH ME.

403
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:18,788
AND THANKS AGAIN
FOR HELPING ME TAKE A SHOWER.

404
00:17:18,788 --> 00:17:23,918
NOW, IS THAT
"NEVER TALKING
ABOUT IT AGAIN"?

405
00:17:23,918 --> 00:17:25,085
HIYA.

406
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:26,921
HEY, JOEY, WE'RE
READY FOR YOU.

407
00:17:26,921 --> 00:17:28,339
UH, JOEY, THIS IS ALEX.

408
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:30,383
HE'S GOING TO BE PLAYING
YOUR SON.

409
00:17:30,383 --> 00:17:32,051
HI, ALEX.

410
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:36,639
AND, UH, AS YOU CAN SEE,
MY HANDS-- NOT IN MY PANTS.

411
00:17:36,639 --> 00:17:37,598
OKAY...

412
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:42,228
ALL RIGHT, UH, ALEX,
NOW, WHEN JOEY SAYS HIS LINE

413
00:17:42,228 --> 00:17:44,438
"TAKE GOOD CARE
OF YOUR MAMA, SON"--

414
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:45,940
THAT'S YOUR CUE TO CRY.

415
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:47,233
GOT IT?

416
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:48,985
ALL RIGHT, LET'S DO THIS.

417
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:55,366
SCENE FIVE, TAKE ONE.

418
00:17:55,366 --> 00:17:57,368
AND... ACTION!

419
00:17:57,368 --> 00:18:00,038
TAKE GOOD CARE
OF YOUR MAMA, SON.

420
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:10,423
TAKE GOOD CARE
OF YOUR MAMA, SON.

421
00:18:13,968 --> 00:18:15,511
COME ON, SON...

422
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:18,681
YOUR MAMA'S GOOD PEOPLE.

423
00:18:18,681 --> 00:18:19,682
CUT!

424
00:18:19,682 --> 00:18:21,559
ALEX, REMEMBER...

425
00:18:21,559 --> 00:18:22,894
YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO CRY.

426
00:18:22,894 --> 00:18:24,520
CAN YOU CRY FOR US
THIS TIME?

427
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,731
OKAY.

428
00:18:26,731 --> 00:18:28,357
ALL RIGHT, FROM THE TOP.

429
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:33,320
SCENE FIVE, TAKE TWO.

430
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:36,032
TAKE 36 IS UP.

431
00:18:36,032 --> 00:18:38,242
Director:
ALL RIGHT, LET'S
TRY THIS AGAIN.

432
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:39,744
ARE YOU READY, JOE?

433
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:41,161
UH, ONE THING--

434
00:18:41,161 --> 00:18:43,081
IS IT ALL RIGHT WITH YOU
IF I... IF I SCREAM

435
00:18:43,081 --> 00:18:44,791
RIGHT UP UNTIL YOU
SAY "ACTION"?

436
00:18:44,791 --> 00:18:46,125
UH, SURE.

437
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:48,753
( screaming )

438
00:18:48,753 --> 00:18:50,004
ACTION!

439
00:18:50,004 --> 00:18:52,673
TAKE GOOD CARE
OF YOUR MAMA, SON.

440
00:18:54,759 --> 00:18:57,053
CUT!
( screaming )

441
00:18:57,053 --> 00:18:58,763
I'M SORRY.

442
00:18:58,763 --> 00:19:00,473
HEY, HEY, JOE, WHY DON'T
YOU LIFT UP YOUR SHIRT?

443
00:19:00,473 --> 00:19:03,476
TAKE A LOOK AT THIS,
KIDDO.

444
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:06,104
( crying )

445
00:19:06,104 --> 00:19:08,188
WE HAVE HIM CRYING, JOHN!

446
00:19:08,188 --> 00:19:10,108
ROLL THE DAMN CAMERAS!

447
00:19:10,108 --> 00:19:12,110
( phone rings )

448
00:19:12,110 --> 00:19:14,612
( ringing )

449
00:19:14,612 --> 00:19:15,613
HELLO?

450
00:19:15,613 --> 00:19:16,948
HELLO, IS ROSS THERE?

451
00:19:16,948 --> 00:19:17,991
UH, NO, HE'S NOT.

452
00:19:17,991 --> 00:19:19,450
CAN I TAKE A MESSAGE?

453
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:21,159
Yes. This is Russell,
Ross's divorce lawyer.

454
00:19:21,159 --> 00:19:23,454
JUST TELL HIM THAT SINCE
I HAVEN'T HEARD FROM HIM

455
00:19:23,454 --> 00:19:25,748
I ASSUME HE'S DECIDED
TO GIVE THE MARRIAGE A TRY.

456
00:19:25,748 --> 00:19:27,374
ROSS GOT MARRIED AGAIN?

457
00:19:27,374 --> 00:19:28,375
( gasping )

458
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:30,920
NO!

459
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:33,089
ALL RIGHT, KEEP GOING.

460
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:36,592
WE ARE PHASING THE ACCENT OUT--
PHASING IT OUT.

461
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:42,015
( unaccented ):
SO WITHOUT RETESTING THE
RESULTS IN THE LA-BOR-ATORY

462
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:45,643
( light accent ):
THE TEAM WOULD NEVER
HAVE I-DENTI-FIED...

463
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:51,231
( unaccented ):
THE INITIAL ERRORS IN THEIR...

464
00:19:51,231 --> 00:19:55,486
( accent ):
CARBON-DATING ANAL-YSIS.

465
00:19:55,486 --> 00:19:59,406
( unaccented ):
WERE THERE ANY QUESTIONS
AT THIS POINT?

466
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:00,533
YES?

467
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:02,368
WHAT'S HAPPENING TO YOUR ACCENT?

468
00:20:04,078 --> 00:20:05,663
( accent ):
COME AGAIN.

469
00:20:05,663 --> 00:20:07,623
WHAT'S-WHAT'S THIS NONSENSE?

470
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,083
( nervous tittering )

471
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:15,006
( unaccented ):
ALL RIGHT, I'M-I'M NOT ENGLISH.

472
00:20:16,049 --> 00:20:19,468
I'M FROM LONG ISLAND.

473
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:22,513
I WAS REALLY NERVOUS,
AND THE ACCENT JUST, UH...

474
00:20:22,513 --> 00:20:24,015
JUST CAME OUT.

475
00:20:24,015 --> 00:20:26,059
( accent ):
I'M SORRY.

476
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:31,605
( unaccented ):
SO, IF WE COULD JUST
GET BACK TO THE LECTURE.

477
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:35,026
UM... WERE THERE ANY QUESTIONS?

478
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:39,363
ABOUT PALEONTOLOGY?

479
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:43,659
ALL RIGHT, LOOK,
I WAS JUST TRYING

480
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:45,745
TO MAKE A GOOD FIRST IMPRESSION.

481
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:48,455
OBVIOUSLY, I SCREWED UP.

482
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:50,208
BUT WHAT YOU GUYS THINK OF ME
IS REALLY IMPORTANT

483
00:20:50,208 --> 00:20:52,960
BECAUSE I'M-I'M HOPING
TO GET A PERMANENT JOB HERE.

484
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:55,880
SO IF YOU JUST GIVE ME
ANOTHER CHANCE

485
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,673
TO MAKE A GOOD IMPRESSION...

486
00:20:57,673 --> 00:21:00,551
ROSS! ARE YOU CRAZY?!

487
00:21:00,551 --> 00:21:01,969
I AM STILL YOUR WIFE?!

488
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:03,930
WHAT, WERE YOU JUST
NEVER GOING TO TELL ME?!

489
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:05,598
WHAT THE HELL IS WRONG
WITH YOU?!!

490
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:09,227
OH! I COULD JUST
KILL YOU!

491
00:21:14,148 --> 00:21:15,775
( heavy accent ):
WELL, 'ELLO, RACHEL!

492
00:21:24,951 --> 00:21:26,452
SO, YOU'VE REALLY
DONE THIS BEFORE?

493
00:21:26,452 --> 00:21:27,787
YEAH, YEAH, YEAH.

494
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:30,372
YOU JUST TAKE A BIG,
BIG SWING, OKAY?

495
00:21:30,372 --> 00:21:31,707
NOW, DON'T HOLD BACK.
OKAY.

496
00:21:34,585 --> 00:21:35,586
HEY!

497
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:37,088
HEY!

498
00:21:37,088 --> 00:21:38,256
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

499
00:21:38,256 --> 00:21:39,506
WE'RE JUST CELEBRATING

500
00:21:39,506 --> 00:21:42,218
THAT JOEY GOT HIS
HEALTH INSURANCE BACK.

501
00:21:42,218 --> 00:21:44,053
OH, ALL RIGHT.

